@ Start

$ Background {&/Game/Melodia/UI/Textures/Figma/T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_SakuraDream.T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_SakuraDream} none 0

- .
  Down by the Dell Spring, a lone Choral Sheep stands knee-deep in sweet clover. Every few seconds it gives a small, indignant bleat—and the bronze bell at its throat rings a single, lonely Middle C.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Companions/ChoralSheep/Audio/sheep_baa_PCC_01.sheep_baa_PCC_01} 0.85

- Melusina
  Oh, look at him. The rest of the flock crossed the Piano Walkway hours ago, and he's still here arguing with the water.

- Sir Melodious
  He is not arguing, Melusina. He is a motif creature of the first octave—a Root-C chorister. And a single note cannot cross a harmony bridge by itself.

- Melusina
  So they just left him behind because he didn't have a third and a fifth? That's ruthless. Even for sheep.

- Sir Melodious
  Watch his fleece. Right now it is quiet pearl-and-blush wool. If you startle him or sing out of key, he will tuck his ears and sulk until Tuesday. How do we approach?

* Kneel in the clover and let him set the tempo first. | -> ApproachSlowly
* Match his bell with a soft Root C on the WaveHarp. | -> CallResponse

<@> ApproachSlowly

- Melusina
  Easy, little soloist. Nobody's here to critique your intonation. Have some dew-clover and tell me where the rest of your choir went.

- .
  The Choral Sheep flicks one ear, sniffs Melusina's outstretched sleeve, and nudges her wrist with its nose. Its bronze bell gives a hopeful chime in Middle C.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Companions/ChoralSheep/Audio/sheep_baa_PCC_small_01.sheep_baa_PCC_small_01} 0.85

- Sir Melodious
  Well done. Creature before technicality—he trusts your silence. Now give him back his keynote so his fleece can wake.

-> CallResponse

<@> CallResponse

- Melusina
  All right. Your note first: Middle C, steady and warm.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Companions/ChoralSheep/Audio/sheep_baa_PCC_lead_01.sheep_baa_PCC_lead_01} 0.9

- .
  As the sheep sings Root C, hidden pearlescent embroidery wakes beneath its Nikki wool—standing-wave nodal rings organizing across its fleece like silver thread woven through blush silk.

- Melusina
  His wool—it's drawing the standing wave! Look at the Chladni rings forming along his flank!

- Sir Melodious
  One note makes a motif, Melusina, but a motif is still lonely. Give him the Major Third—sing the E above his C!

* Sing the E-natural third and let Sir Melodious crown the Fifth (G). | -> BuildTriad
* Hold the E-natural third gently so the sheep leads the resolution. | -> BuildTriad

<@> BuildTriad

- Melusina
  Do... Mi...

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_halfsong_01.mel_halfsong_01} 0.9
      $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Companions/ChoralSheep/Audio/sheep_baa_PCE_lead_01.sheep_baa_PCE_lead_01} 0.85

- .
  The fleece pattern shifts—two frequencies interfering in delicate lilac filigree across the wool. Perched on Melusina's forearm, Sir Melodious lifts his crest and whistles a crystal-clear G.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Companions/ChoralSheep/Audio/sheep_baa_PCG_lead_01.sheep_baa_PCG_lead_01} 0.9

- .
  C — E — G. The triad locks. Diamond wool-motes spiral upward from the sheep's back as the interference resolves into a single, luminous harmonic field—rippling outward from the creature into the dell water and ringing the third brass door of the Morning House!

$ %ReactiveToMusic.TryBeginHarmonize
$ Notify melodia:stat:intent.choral_sheep.call_response:melodia_harmony:2
$ Notify melodia:flag:flag.companion.choral_sheep_recruited:true

- Sir Melodious
  Creature, Motif, Harmony, World! Look how the pond and the house answer when the chord stabilizes!

- Melusina
  You weren't out of tune at all—you were just waiting for a trio. Come on, little C-Root. Let's go open the high balcony.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_reunion_01.mel_reunion_01} 0.9

$ Notify melodia:questcomplete:quest.companion.choral_sheep:flag.companion.choral_sheep_completed:reward.companion.choral_sheep:intent.companion.choral_sheep.complete:checkpoint.companion.choral_sheep.complete

@ Finish

- .
  The Choral Sheep trots happily into Melusina's ensemble, its Chladni fleece glowing in C-major resonance as the third chamber door of the Morning House rises open.

$ End
